abstract: 'Qi zheng lue shu (editorial translation: Brief accounts of remarkable cases)
  contains case records and institutional documents associated with John Glasgow Kerr
  and the Medical Missionary Society hospital at Canton (Guangzhou). It includes cases
  and captions concerning stones, tumours and other conditions, together with hospital
  reports, accounts, attendance figures, organizational business and publishing notices.
  It supports histories of medicine, medical missions, translation, charity and medical
  illustration. The catalogue date 1864–1868 is recorded separately from imprints
  dated 1866 and 1868, a preface dated 1869 and an appendix dated 1873. This version
  provides JSON, TXT and TEI for 91 original printed faces, unit-level links to the
  source, uncertainty records and a separately labelled readable derivative. The transcription
  is AI-assisted: the earlier 60 faces retain independent AI reading comparison and
  image review; the added 31 faces are initial transcription of this witness. Uncertain
  readings remain marked; expert review has not been performed.'
